From: Lunar Linux build audit
Subject: [PATCH] Remove avoidable build noise in Nim 2.2.10 tools

A standard Nim 2.2.10 build reports several avoidable unused/duplicate
import diagnostics and three dead declarations in the legacy IC test helper.

The changes are intentionally mechanical:
- remove unused imports from tools/deps.nim and nimsuggest/nimsuggest.nim;
- avoid duplicate strutils/gitutils imports caused by categories.nim being
  included into testament.nim;
- remove two unused IC option constants and one unused local template.

The IC helper declarations are specific to the 2.2.10-era implementation;
current devel has since replaced that code. The import cleanups remain useful
independently.

diff --git a/tools/deps.nim b/tools/deps.nim
--- ./tools/deps.nim
+++ ./tools/deps.nim
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-import std/[os, uri, strformat, strutils]
+import std/[os, uri, strformat]
 import std/private/gitutils
 
 when defined(nimPreviewSlimSystem):
diff --git a/nimsuggest/nimsuggest.nim b/nimsuggest/nimsuggest.nim
--- ./nimsuggest/nimsuggest.nim
+++ ./nimsuggest/nimsuggest.nim
@@ -8,11 +8,8 @@
 #
 
 import compiler/renderer
 import compiler/types
-import compiler/trees
-import compiler/wordrecg
-import compiler/sempass2
 import strformat
